# Line-ending policy. The repo is developed on Windows (core.autocrlf=true) but
# shell scripts run inside Linux containers (busybox sh in the backup sidecar,
# alpine in CI). CRLF endings break those shells (`set -o pipefail\r` errors), so
# force LF on everything that is executed by a POSIX shell or copied into an image.
*.sh            text eol=lf
Dockerfile*     text eol=lf
*.yml           text eol=lf
*.yaml          text eol=lf

# Windows-side scripts stay CRLF.
*.ps1           text eol=crlf

# Let Git auto-detect the rest.
*               text=auto
